{sec("pale", f"""{split("", f"Regulated. Audited.<br>Connected{G}", "EMFI operates through specialist legal entities and works with established professional firms and market infrastructure. The relationship matters, but so does the precise role each organisation performs.")}<div class="ledger mt">{evh}</div><p class="fine" style="margin-top:18px">Regulator names are presented as text references, not regulator logos or endorsements. {T("Third-party roles and audit scopes must be checked against current contracts and appointment letters. Use approved official wordmark files only where permission is available")}</p>""")}
{sec("white", f"""{split("", f"Client Assets.<br>Accounted For{G}", "Safeguarding client assets is a continuing operational responsibility. In the UK, the FCA&rsquo;s Client Assets Sourcebook sets requirements for client money and safe custody assets.")}<div class="big3 mt"><div class="it rv"><b>CASS 7</b><h3>Client Money</h3><p>Applicable arrangements include segregation, records, reconciliations and acknowledgement arrangements with the banks holding client money. The statutory trust framework is designed to protect client money if a firm fails.</p></div><div class="it rv"><b>CASS 6</b><h3>Safe Custody Assets</h3><p>Applicable requirements cover safekeeping, ownership rights, records and reconciliations, helping distinguish client assets from the firm&rsquo;s own assets and those of other clients.</p></div><div class="it rv"><b>DIFC</b><h3>Separate client asset framework</h3><p>EMFI Capital (DIFC) Limited is subject to the DFSA&rsquo;s applicable client asset requirements. These are separate from the FCA&rsquo;s CASS rules.</p></div></div><p class="fine" style="margin-top:24px">Segregation, records and reconciliations are designed to reduce specific custody and client asset risks. They do not eliminate investment losses, banking or depository failures, counterparty risk or every risk arising on insolvency.</p>""")}
{sec("navy", f"""{split("", f"Know What<br>You Pay{G}", "A fee schedule should make the economics of the relationship understandable before you transact.")}<p class="lead rv" style="margin-top:22px;max-width:none">EMFI&rsquo;s commercial arrangements can include custody fees, monthly minimums, execution and ticket charges, account or service fees and third-party infrastructure costs. The applicable schedule should identify the charging basis, relevant thresholds, currency, minimums and any pass-through items so you can understand what you are paying and why.</p><div class="ledger mt"><div class="lr rv"><strong>Custody</strong><span>Basis-point rate, asset basis, tier and any monthly minimum.</span></div><div class="lr rv"><strong>Execution</strong><span>Ticket charges, market or venue charges and applicable minimums.</span></div><div class="lr rv"><strong>Settlement &amp; infrastructure</strong><span>Depository, market infrastructure and third-party charges passed through where applicable.</span></div><div class="lr rv"><strong>Cash and other services</strong><span>Applicable interest, account and service charges, including the calculation basis.</span></div></div><p class="fine" style="margin-top:18px">The actual rates and minimums depend on the agreed commercial schedule, account, service, instrument and client circumstances. This page is not a fee quotation. {T("Publish a link to the approved fee schedule only after Compliance and commercial approval")}</p>""")}
{sec("white", f"""{split("", f"In the Market.<br>In the Conversation{G}", "Actual external coverage, interviews and attributed commentary. Every publication mark takes the visitor to the underlying source.")}<div class="cards mt"><div class="card rv"><h3>Publication / outlet</h3><p>Article headline, named EMFI contributor and publication date. {T("Replace with verified article")}</p></div><div class="card rv"><h3>Publication / outlet</h3><p>Interview or quoted commentary, with a direct source link. {T("Replace with verified article")}</p></div><div class="card rv"><h3>Independent recognition</h3><p>Specific award, category, year and awarding organisation. {T("Replace with verified award")}</p></div></div><p class="fine" style="margin-top:22px">{T("Do not display publications or awards merely because EMFI has a profile or indirect association. Confirm the quotation, date, source and permission to use each logo")}</p>""")}
